# railway.ts is infrastructure-as-code and belongs in git; README.md here
# is just the CLI's own boilerplate note.
.railway/README.md

# Next.js writes this on every build/dev run, and its contents follow the
# active distDir — ".next" after a production build, ".next-dev" after
# `pnpm dev`. Tracking it meant it flip-flopped in git forever. Every build
# regenerates it, and typecheck passes without it on a clean checkout, so it
# is a build artifact, not source.
next-env.d.ts

